r utilities whose primary output is a file rather than stdout (sponge, cp, mv)\n      - path: pkg/testutils/runner_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for RunDiffTests (passing and failing cases), TimestampNormalizer (pattern replacement), file-state comparison (matching and divergent files), timeout behavior\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Define DiffTest struct per prd001-testutils R1.1-R1.4. Fields: Name (string, used as\n          t.Run subtest name), Args ([]string, command-line arguments passed to both binaries),\n          Stdin ([]byte, nil means no stdin/immediate EOF), Env ([]string, nil means inherit test\n          process environment), ExitCode (int, expected exit code -- not used for comparison between\n          binaries, only documents intent), Normalize ([]Normalize, nil or empty means no\n          normalization), WorkDir (string, optional working directory; empty means create per-test\n          temp directory), ExpectedFiles (map[string][]byte, nil means no file-state check).\n          Define Normalize as func([]byte) []byte.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n          per prd001-testutils R2.1-R2.5. For each DiffTest, invoke both goBinary and refBinary\n          with identical Args, Stdin, and Env. Capture stdout and stderr into separate byte buffers\n          and record the exit code from each binary independently. Impose a configurable timeout\n          (default 10 seconds) on each binary invocation using exec.CommandContext with\n          context.WithTimeout. If either binary exceeds the timeout, fail the test with a message\n          naming the binary and its args. When WorkDir is empty, create a temporary directory via\n          t.TempDir() for each binary invocation. Produce no output to stdout or stderr during a\n          passing test run (use t.Errorf/t.Fatalf only on failure).\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement comparison and reporting per prd001-testutils R3.1-R3.6. Before comparing,\n          apply the DiffTest.Normalize slice (each function in order) to both binaries' stdout and\n          stderr. Compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte; any difference is a test failure. Compare\n          normalized stderr byte-for-byte; any difference is a test failure. Compare exit codes\n          exactly; a difference is a test failure. On any divergence, report in the failure message:\n          the DiffTest.Args, the Stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), the reference\n          binary stdout, the Go binary stdout, the reference binary stderr, the Go binary stderr,\n          and both exit codes. Run each DiffTest as a named subtest via t.Run(test.Name, ...) so\n          individual failures are identifiable in go test output.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement normalization hooks per prd001-testutils R4.1-R4.3. Provide a\n          TimestampNormalizer (a Normalize function) that uses regexp to replace common strftime\n          timestamp patterns with the fixed string \"TIMESTAMP\". Patterns to match: \"Mon DD HH:MM:SS\"\n          (e.g., \"Feb 19 14:05:32\"), \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS\" (e.g., \"2024-02-19T14:05:32\"),\n          \"HH:MM:SS\" standalone elapsed-time format (e.g., \"00:00:05\"). Provide a\n          ComposeNormalizers(norms ...Normalize) Normalize function that returns a single Normalize\n          applying each norm in order. When the DiffTest.Normalize slice is nil or empty, no\n          normalization is applied.\n      - id: R5\n        text: |\n          Implement file-state comparison per prd001-testutils R5.1-R5.2. When\n          DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is non-nil, after both binaries have exited, for each key in\n          ExpectedFiles read the file at that path (relative to the binary's working directory)\n          from both the Go binary's and the reference binary's working directories. Compare file\n          contents byte-for-byte. Report file-content divergence in the same format as stdout\n          divergence (file path, expected content from reference binary workdir, actual content\n          from Go binary workdir).\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          DiffTest is the primary exported type; its definition goes in difftest.go per the project\n          naming convention (Go packages name the primary source file after the primary exported\n          type, not the package name -- testutils/testutils.go is forbidden).\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Use exec.CommandContext with context.WithTimeout for the 10-second default timeout per\n          prd001-testutils R2.3. Extract the exit code from the *exec.ExitError type assertion on\n          the error returned by cmd.Run(). When the context deadline is exceeded, report timeout\n          with the binary path and args.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Run each DiffTest as t.Run(test.Name, func(t *testing.T) { ... }) per prd001-testutils\n          R3.6 so that individual test case failures are identifiable in go test -v output and can\n          be filtered with go test -run.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          TimestampNormalizer compiles its regexps once at package init time (or via sync.Once) and\n          reuses them across calls. The replacement string is the literal \"TIMESTAMP\" for all\n          patterns per prd001-testutils AC3.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: |\n          A cmd/ package can define a []DiffTest slice and call RunDiffTests(t, goBinary,\n          refBinary, tests) from a TestXxx function with no other setup beyond building the\n          binaries (prd001-testutils AC1).\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          A passing test run produces no output on stdout or stderr. A failing test prints the\n          triggering args, stdin (truncated), and both binaries' stdout, stderr, and exit code\n          via t.Errorf (prd001-testutils AC2).\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          TimestampNormalizer replaces strftime-formatted timestamps (e.g., \"Feb 19 12:34:56\")\n          with the fixed placeholder \"TIMESTAMP\" so that differential tests with wall-clock\n          timestamps can pass despite timing differences (prd001-testutils AC3).\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          A DiffTest with a non-nil ExpectedFiles field correctly fails when the Go binary writes\n          different file content than the reference binary to the same relative path\n          (prd001-testutils AC4).\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          A DiffTest where either binary exceeds the 10-second timeout fails with a clear timeout\n          message (naming the binary and args) rather than hanging the test run\n          (prd001-testutils AC5).\n      - id: AC6\n        text: |\n          All pkg/testutils code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint\n          (prd001-testutils AC6).\n      - id: AC7\n        text: go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
